          "normalized_title": "Why Are So Many New Fathers Dying? Scientists Say the U.S. Has a Dangerous Blind Spot",
          "normalized_summary": "A new study examining paternal mortality data in Georgia found that 60% of the deaths were preventable. It took nearly a century for maternal mortality in the United States to be acknowledged, pushed out of focus, and then recognized again as a major public health emergency. Paternal mortality has followed a very different path. Research [...]",
